{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/946108-celerity-vs-celerity","id":946108,"title":"Celerity vs Celerity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T06:07:31-07:00","id":946108,"title":"Celerity vs Celerity","content":"Right so had a question on what happens when two clerity bunnies go toe to toe specifically regarding the interrupt portions.<br /> <br /> So they are fighting. <br /> <br /> Vamp A goes to attack, B activates celerity to interrupt, A then activates celerity to interrupt the interrupt.<br /> <br /> There are 3 outcomes to this that i can see.<br /> <br /> 1) It states you cant interrupt a reflective action, using celerity is reflexive so cant be interrupted at all.<br /> <br /> 2) it becomes a clash of wills to determine whos interrupt takes place<br /> <br /> 3) Because you are taking an 'instant action' using celerity it stops being reflexive and therefore you can respond with an interrupt to an interupt.<br /> <br /> Has their been any official ruling on this before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:07:34-07:00","id":946131,"title":"","content":"Yes, the second one. It is a clash of wills as stated in the beginning of the chapter when it talks about two supernatural powers with the same effect take place at the same moment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Celerity + BP vs. Celerity + BP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-08-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:19:02-07:00","id":946138,"title":"","content":"I would go with not being able to interrupt an interrupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:46:13-07:00","id":946164,"title":"","content":"Vampire A already declared his instant action. Interrupting IS your action for that turn so unless vampire A specifically predicated his attack in anticipation of vampire B using celerity to interrupt it,(at that point it's a clash of wills) the only thing they did is waste time and interrupts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:15:43-07:00","id":946175,"title":"","content":"This is a great question. This actually came up in my game 2 weeks ago. Player shot at NPC. NPC interrupted that shot with celerity by moving, then took his turn to attack Player. Player Interrupted the attack by moving. <br /> <br /> I didnt think you should be allowed to interrupt an interrupt, but ultimately, since she didnt move. I allowed the clash of wills, Player won, so player moved. NPC missed. Which sort of negated both their turns.<br /> <br /> But I am really open to hearing more on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:25:50-07:00","id":946182,"title":"","content":"I think a clash of will is needed and necessary. Or the best tactic would be wait for the enemy action then interrupt without the possibility to avoid that even with celerity. That's could result in an eternal waiting fight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-08-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:40:46-07:00","id":946231,"title":"","content":"Celerity *explicitly* cant interrupt a reflexive action or surprise attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:22:02-07:00","id":946260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/946108-celerity-vs-celerity?p=946231#post946231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity *explicitly* cant interrupt a reflexive action or surprise attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably it's not the Reflexive activation of Celerity you're interrupting, it's the Instant action they interrupt your action with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I could have sworn <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> had said this was possible and provoked a Clash of Wills during Requiem 2e open development, but I can't find it. It might have been on the old forums. Oh, well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:34:39-07:00","id":946272,"title":"","content":"Hum. Technically speaking you are correct. It says uts an interrupt, not a reflexive action. I wouldnt play it that way, but it is a valid read of the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:50:20-07:00","id":946428,"title":"","content":"If two vampires try to interrupt the same action you get a clash of wills to determine who's first. <br /> <br /> If it's two vampires who want to fight each other in same turn, then I'd most likely lean on what tsusasi said. Except that the vampire who just now interupted, might still do a move action (unless he used up that one). At that point vampire B does his declared action (with which he interupted A), and then vampire A does his declared action if it's still possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:08:28-07:00","id":946656,"title":"","content":"Rose or David did comment about the clash of wills on the old forums, I remember it too Charlaquin. Basically if one tries to interrupt the other, and then the first goes to interrupt the interrupt, they said it was a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:12:44-07:00","id":946659,"title":"","content":"I thought this situation was a poster child for Clash of Wills. If it helps, Mage has similar power - Acceleration - and it states that when two powers that manipulate the initiative stack (either by forcibly putting you on top, or by interrupting another's action) clash, they Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}